KCAT TECHNOLOGY REFERENCE
=========================
Local news & events monitor for Kannapolis, NC
Project: kspider / KCAT Dashboard


─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LANGUAGE & RUNTIME
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Python 3.9+
    Core language for all backend crawling, data storage, and CLI.
    Requires 3.9+ for type-hint syntax used throughout the codebase.

  JavaScript (ES2020, no framework)
    All dashboard interactivity — rendering, filtering, localStorage,
    calendar, .ics download, weather, clock, toast notifications.
    Zero external JS dependencies; runs entirely in the browser.

  HTML5 / CSS3
    Single-file dashboard (kcat.html) generated by kspider export.
    CSS custom properties (variables) power the dark theme.
    SVG used for the analog clock, cat logo, and all icons.


─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PYTHON PACKAGES (third-party)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  feedparser
    Parses RSS and Atom feeds. Used by: Google News, Google Alerts,
    Cabarrus Compass (Substack), Independent Tribune (BLOX CMS).

  beautifulsoup4 (bs4)
    HTML scraping and parsing. Used by: Bing web search, Bing News,
    City of Kannapolis news page.

  lxml
    Fast XML/HTML parser backend for BeautifulSoup. Also required
    for system-level XML processing on some platforms.

  duckduckgo_search (ddgs)
    DuckDuckGo search library. Uses ddgs.news() for dated results
    from DuckDuckGo and DuckDuckGo Images sources.


─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PYTHON STANDARD LIBRARY (key modules)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  sqlite3       Local database for storing all crawl results and run history
  subprocess    Spawns curl for HTTP fetching (bypasses Python 3.9 TLS issues)
  argparse      CLI argument parsing (kspider search, export, results, runs)
  select        Non-blocking stdin for countdown timer in --loop mode
  base64        Decodes Bing redirect URLs (base64url-encoded destinations)
  html          HTML entity unescaping (unescape)
  re            Regular expressions for HTML stripping, date extraction
  json          API response parsing (CivicClerk, WordPress, etc.)
  datetime      Timestamp parsing, ISO formatting, timezone handling
  calendar      timegm() for UTC struct_time → epoch conversion
  urllib.parse  URL parsing, query string extraction, quote/urlencode


─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SYSTEM TOOLS
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  curl
    Used via subprocess for all HTTP fetching in sources that require
    a real browser User-Agent or encounter Python TLS compatibility
    issues. Required on all platforms (included with macOS/Windows 10+).

  zip
    Used for creating project backups (kcat_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.zip).


─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DATABASE
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  SQLite3
    File-based relational database at ~/.kspider/results.db
    Tables: results, search_runs, blocked_urls
    No database server required — embedded in Python standard library.
    Deduplication handled at export time (dedupe=True in server.py).


─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DATA SOURCES & APIs
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  CivicClerk REST API
    Endpoint: kannapolisnc.api.civicclerk.com/v1/Events
    Returns upcoming city meetings with agenda status, location, and
    published files. Unauthenticated JSON API with OData filtering.

  City of Kannapolis News (HTML scraping)
    URL: kannapolisnc.gov/news
    DNN (DotNetNuke) CMS. Scraped with BeautifulSoup via curl.
    Parses div.article > div.articleHeadline, div.articleAuthor,
    div.articleEntry for title, date, and snippet.

  Public Notices — Concord Independent Tribune
    URL: civicpublicnotice.com portal
    Scraped for legal notices specific to Kannapolis/Cabarrus County.

  Cabarrus Compass (Substack RSS)
    Feed: cabarruscompass.com/feed
    RSS parsed directly with feedparser. 90-day window.

  Independent Tribune (BLOX CMS RSS)
    Feed: independenttribune.com/search/?f=rss&t=article&q=kannapolis
    Fetched via curl (site blocks non-browser User-Agents), then
    parsed with feedparser from the response string.

  Salisbury Post (WordPress REST API)
    Endpoint: salisburypost.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts?search=kannapolis
    WordPress JSON API. Strips HTML from title/excerpt fields.
    Returns featured media URL for thumbnail images. 30-day window.

  Google Alerts RSS
    Feed: google.com/alerts/feeds/[user-id]/[alert-id]
    RSS parsed with feedparser. Google redirect URLs unwrapped via
    the url= query parameter. Delivers fresh Kannapolis content
    whenever Google indexes it.

  Google News RSS
    Feed: news.google.com/rss/search?q=Kannapolis
    Standard RSS via feedparser. Returns recent news articles.

  Bing Web Search (HTML scraping)
    URL: bing.com/search?q=...
    Scraped with BeautifulSoup. Redirect URLs (bing.com/ck/a?...)
    decoded via base64url decoding of the u= parameter (a1 prefix
    stripped) to obtain stable destination URLs.

  Bing News (HTML scraping)
    URL: bing.com/news/search?q=...
    Scraped similarly to Bing web. Returns news-specific results
    with publication dates extracted from snippets.

  DuckDuckGo News (duckduckgo_search)
    Uses ddgs.news() with timelimit="d" for fresh, dated results.
    Throttled to avoid rate limiting (2s between requests).

  DuckDuckGo Images (duckduckgo_search)
    Uses ddgs.images() for image results. Returns thumbnail URLs.

  Facebook Public Posts
    Scraped from public Facebook pages.

  Instagram Public Posts
    Scraped from public Instagram profiles.

  YouTube
    Video search results for Kannapolis-related content.


─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
EXTERNAL APIS (dashboard / frontend)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Open-Meteo Weather API (free, no key required)
    Endpoint: api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast
    Coordinates: 35.4874°N, 80.6217°W (Kannapolis, NC)
    Returns current temperature, apparent temperature, and weather
    condition code (WMO standard). Polled every 10 minutes.
    No API key required.


─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DASHBOARD BROWSER FEATURES
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  localStorage
    Persists dismissed URLs (kspider_dismissed), snoozed CivicClerk
    meeting URLs (kspider_snoozed), and UI state (kspider_state:
    source filter, query filter, text search, view mode).
    Data is browser-specific and does not sync across devices.

  Blob + URL.createObjectURL
    Generates downloadable .ics calendar files in-browser for
    CivicClerk meeting events. No server round-trip required.

  navigator.clipboard.writeText
    Copies article URLs to clipboard for the Facebook Share feature.

  Fetch API
    Used for the Open-Meteo weather data requests.

  SVG
    Analog clock (animated via JS), cat mascot logo with blink
    animation, calendar icon, and all chip action icons.

  CSS Custom Properties
    Dark theme variables (--bg, --surface, --accent, --text, etc.)
    and per-source badge colors (--c-civicclerk, --c-bing, etc.).


─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PACKAGING & DISTRIBUTION
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  pyproject.toml
    PEP 517/518 build configuration. Defines package metadata,
    dependencies, and the kspider console entry point.

  pip install -e .
    Editable (development) install. Changes to source files take
    effect immediately without reinstalling.

  Entry point: kspider → kspider.cli:main
    Installed to ~/Library/Python/3.x/bin/kspider (macOS) or
    %APPDATA%\Python\Scripts\kspider.exe (Windows).


